{"title":"2009 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Construct a square on one side of an equilateral triangle. On one non-adjacent side of the square, construct a regular pentagon, as shown. On a non-adjacent side of the pentagon, construct a hexagon. Continue to construct regular polygons in the same way, until you construct an octagon. How many sides does the resulting polygon have?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/a/d4a192b1c509fea9e4f0b63b29b58c056ff0a1ab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(linewidth(0.6)); pair O=origin, A=(0,1), B=A+1*dir(60), C=(1,1), D=(1,0), E=D+1*dir(-72), F=E+1*dir(-144), G=O+1*dir(-108); draw(O--A--B--C--D--E--F--G--cycle); draw(O--D, dashed); draw(A--C, dashed);[/asy]\" width=\"122\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/0/4e0b1f95b3aaeb016df7875ead93316d4fb8fb28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 21 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 23 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 25 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 27 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 29$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Of the six shapes used to create the polygon, the triangle and octagon are adjacent to the others on one side, and the others are adjacent on two sides. In the triangle and octagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/1/e61e5de38472b0eb33d5b5c8637cdf45cc4832ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+8-2(1)=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" /> sides are on the outside of the final polygon. In the other shapes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5ab41498d77e8738290f3f424f336d75edb52a62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+5+6+7-4(2) = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"200\" height=\"18\" /> sides are on the outside. The resulting polygon has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/b/64b2576dfb6802033431b8998b6c1a2728910883.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9+14 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 23}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"137\" height=\"28\" /> sides.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can quickly see a pattern if we draw out the other shapes. Every shape will have two of its sides taken out except the triangle and octagon. We can then make the expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/5/2a57db35f42f58ec773d7071eb8aa9a46e049469.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+2+3+4+5+7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"165\" height=\"14\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/b/cdbe38ae96cfecd01248c5a34519c2c2932ea79f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 23}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~Trex226\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/eG8w13-3S8M\">https://youtu.be/eG8w13-3S8M</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8\" title=\"2009 AMC 8\"